1.text:
{}
On the normal infinite/19×19 interpretation the white D1-D2 group has the
three liberties E1 E2 D3 and White is not forced to play D3.

The black corner consists of

* C1–C2 : {B1,B2}
* A2   : {A1,A3,B2}
* B3–B4 : {A3,A4,B2}

with B2 the common liberty.  B1 and B2 are a mutual atari:

* W B1 → … B B2 merges A2,B3–B4,C1–C2 to A1 A3 A4 B1 and W B1 is itself
  in atari on A1, B A1 removes the attacker;
* W B2 → W B2 is 1-lib on B1 and B B1 captures at once.

A1,A3,A4 are all immediately capturable or are met by the connecting
move B2.  After 1.W A4 Black has

* 2.B A3   – W A4 is now 1-lib on A5 and the A2-B3-B4 complex is on A1 B2;
* 2.B B2   – the three black groups merge to A1 A3 A4 B1 and W B1 is
  in atari on A1;
* 2.B A1   – C1–C2 is put on B2 and A2/B3–B4 on A3 B2;
* 2.B B1   – C1–C2 is put on B2.

In every line Black can either capture the attacking white stone on
A1/B1/A4 or connect on B2 and restore ≥2 liberties to the merged
A2-B3-B4-C1-C2 formation, so no first white move puts Black in zugzwang
and forces a capture.  The same mutual atari and recapture phenomena
obtain for B1,B2,A1,A3,A4 and for any other point.  Hence there is no
first move that guarantees a capture against best defence.

No forced kill exists on the usual board interpretation.

