7.text:
{}

On the standard infinite/19×19 board the corner formation is

* A2 {A1,A3,B2}
* B3–B4 {A3,A4,B2}
* C1–C2 {B1,B2}

White D1–D2 is {E1,E2,D3} and is not forced. B2 is the common liberty of the three black groups and B1/B2 is a mutual atari with C1–C2.

1.W B1 → 2.B B2 is legal. B2 joins A2,B3–B4,C1–C2 to M = A2 B2 B3 B4 C1 C2 with liberties A1 A3 A4 and leaves W B1 with the single liberty A1. 3.B A1 captures the attacker. The same snap-back holds for 1.W B2 → 2.B B1 captures at once.

1.W A1 → 2.B B1 captures, 1.W A3 → 2.B A4 captures.

1.W A4 puts W A4 on {A3,A5}. 2.B A5 is legal, A5 has A6 and B5. After 2.B A5 W A4 is on the single liberty A3 and W A3 is suicide. 3.B A3 removes the probe. The alternative defences 2.B A3, 2.B B2, 2.B A1, 2.B B1 all keep the A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 formation on ≥2 liberties A1 A3 A4 B1 and allow Black to capture the probing white stone on A1/B1/A3.

Hence every first white point in the neighbourhood A1 A3 A4 B1 B2 is either an immediate snap-back or a mutual atari that Black answers with …B B2 and/or …B A5/A3, and the merged black group can always be kept on ≥2 liberties while the probing stone is recaptured. No first move puts Black in zugzwang and forces a capture of any black group against best defence.

